From: Jan Benedikt <karagos01@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gstsink: Don't let GstGL terminate GDK's EGLDisplay on Wayland

On Wayland the sink hands GstGL a GstGLDisplayWayland for GDK's
wl_display. GstGL derives a GstGLDisplayEGL from it on demand, and since
EGL returns one EGLDisplay per native display, that is the same
EGLDisplay GDK renders with. That GstGLDisplayEGL is not marked foreign,
so when the last media stream is disposed it calls eglTerminate() and
every GL context of the application stops working: the next
gdk_gl_context_make_current() fails with EGL_BAD_DISPLAY and GSK
crashes on a NULL context.

GNOME Snapshot hits this after each shutter sound, crashing on the
second picture on a Mali-G615 (panthor) phone running Phosh.

Mark the derived GstGLDisplayEGL as foreign, like the X11 path does by
wrapping GDK's EGLDisplay with gst_gl_display_egl_new_with_egl_display().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Jan Benedikt <karagos01@gmail.com>
---
--- a/gtk/media/gtkgstsink.c
+++ b/gtk/media/gtkgstsink.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
 #include <gst/d3d12/gstd3d12.h>
 #endif
 
-#if GST_GL_HAVE_PLATFORM_EGL && (GST_GL_HAVE_WINDOW_WIN32 || GST_GL_HAVE_WINDOW_X11)
+#if GST_GL_HAVE_PLATFORM_EGL && (GST_GL_HAVE_WINDOW_WIN32 || GST_GL_HAVE_WINDOW_X11 || GST_GL_HAVE_WINDOW_WAYLAND)
 #include <gst/gl/egl/gstgldisplay_egl.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -891,6 +891,23 @@
 
           wayland_display = gdk_wayland_display_get_wl_display (display);
           self->gst_display = GST_GL_DISPLAY (gst_gl_display_wayland_new_with_display (wayland_display));
+
+          /* GstGL creates a GstGLDisplayEGL for the wl_display on demand.
+           * EGL hands out one EGLDisplay per native display, so that is the
+           * very EGLDisplay GDK renders with, and GstGL would eglTerminate()
+           * it once the sink goes away, taking every GL context of the
+           * application down with it. GDK owns the EGLDisplay: mark it
+           * foreign. */
+          {
+            GstGLDisplayEGL *display_egl;
+
+            display_egl = gst_gl_display_egl_from_gl_display (self->gst_display);
+            if (display_egl)
+              {
+                gst_gl_display_egl_set_foreign (display_egl, TRUE);
+                gst_object_unref (display_egl);
+              }
+          }
           self->gst_gdk_context = gst_gl_context_new_wrapped (self->gst_display, gl_handle, platform, gl_api);
         }
       else
